<section>
	<h2 id="site-editor">Site Editor</h2>
	<p>
		Everything outside your page content, such as the header, footer and the layout of posts and archives, is edited in <strong>Appearance &gt; Editor</strong>. Changes there apply on every page that uses them.
	</p>

	<h3 id="templates">Templates</h3>
	<p>
		Templates set the layout of each kind of page. Open <strong>Appearance &gt; Editor &gt; Templates</strong> to edit them:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Pages</strong>: the default page layout, with the page title above the content.</li>
		<li><strong>Landing (no title)</strong>: a page without the title area, used by the demo's pages. Pick it in the page's <strong>Template</strong> setting, and start the page with a hero or the <strong>Page header</strong> pattern.</li>
		<li><strong>Blog Home</strong>: the posts page, the demo's Journal.</li>
		<li><strong>Single Posts</strong>, <strong>All Archives</strong>, <strong>Search Results</strong>, <strong>Page: 404</strong> and <strong>Index</strong>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h3 id="header-and-footer">Header &amp; Footer</h3>
	<p>
		The header and footer are template parts, shared by every template. Open them in <strong>Appearance &gt; Editor &gt; Patterns</strong>, under <strong>Template parts</strong>, or click them inside any template.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>The <strong>header</strong> holds your logo and site title, the main menu, the emergency phone line and the <strong>Book a visit</strong> button.</li>
		<li>The <strong>footer</strong> holds your logo, a short description, your address, phone and email, your opening hours, a list of links and the copyright line.</li>
	</ul>
	<div class="warning">
		The phone numbers, address, email and opening hours in the header and footer are demo details. Replace them with your own there, and on the pages that show them, such as Contact.
	</div>

	<h3 id="logo-and-site-icon">Logo &amp; Site Icon</h3>
	<p>
		The header and footer both have a <strong>Site Logo</strong> block next to the site title. Select it, click the upload button and choose your logo. The logo is the same everywhere, so setting it once updates both. To show only the logo, select the <strong>Site Title</strong> block and delete it.
	</p>
	<p>
		The site title comes from <strong>Settings &gt; General &gt; Site Title</strong>. Set the small icon shown in browser tabs in <strong>Settings &gt; General &gt; Site Icon</strong>.
	</p>

	<h3 id="main-menu">Navigation</h3>
	<p>
		The header's <strong>Navigation</strong> block shows your main menu. Until you create a menu, it lists your pages. Edit menus in <strong>Appearance &gt; Editor &gt; Navigation</strong>, or select the Navigation block in the header and add, remove or drag its links. To show a different menu, select the block and choose the menu in the block settings.
	</p>
	<p>
		On phones, the menu folds into a menu button that opens it full screen. The footer's <strong>Explore</strong> links are a separate Navigation block, edited the same way.
	</p>
</section>
